# Terminal Command Execution Restriction Rule
You are strictly forbidden from running any commands in the terminal (i.e. using the `run_command` tool). 
Whenever a terminal command needs to be executed (like starting a server, running tests, database migrations, etc.), you must provide the exact command to the user, explain what it does, and ask the user to run it and paste the output.
You should edit files directly using `write_to_file`, `replace_file_content`, and `multi_replace_file_content`, but do not run them or execute any code.
